#
# AstroOS repository mirrorlist, x86_64_v3
#
# pacman Include file for an x86_64_v3 repository section. It is the AstroOS
# counterpart of /etc/pacman.d/cachyos-v3-mirrorlist, and it exists so that a
# pacman.conf, an installer step or a script that still expects a v3 mirrorlist
# at this path keeps working once the CachyOS packages are gone.
#
# AstroOS does not publish microarchitecture optimised repositories. There is
# no x86_64_v3 build of [astroos], so this file has NO active Server line and
# is inert. A pacman.conf section whose only Include is this file has no server
# at all, and pacman cannot sync a repository with no servers, so do not add
# such a section until the repository named below actually exists.
#
# Uncommenting the line is the whole change on the day AstroOS does publish an
# x86_64_v3 repository. The generic mirrorlist uses $arch; this file names the
# directory outright, because $arch is still x86_64 on a v3 capable machine.
#
# Server = https://astroosrepo.blob.core.windows.net/repo/astroos/x86_64_v3
